{
  "format": 1,
  "comment": [
    "Shared key-value dialect goldens, replayed by the C ABI test (bindings/c/src/kv.rs), the Python, Node and WASM binding tests and by tests/kv_dialect_goldens.rs against vlite-mcp and vlite-shell, so that the surfaces cannot drift apart.",
    "Every sequence starts on a fresh database whose default collection has one dimension. `collections` adds named collections. A `read_only` sequence first applies `seed` (requests) to a writable handle of a file and then replays `steps` on a read-only handle of that file.",
    "A step is {name, request, result | error}. `request` is a key-value request in the dialect of the MCP/shell tools (`op` is get, put, delete or list); `result` is the exact result JSON and `error` the stable error code. Messages are not pinned.",
    "`skip` lists surfaces that do not replay a sequence or step (c, python, node, wasm, mcp, shell). `typed: false` marks requests the typed bindings cannot express (unknown fields, wrong JSON types, malformed base64 or decimals): only the raw JSON dialect replays them.",
    "Templates: in a request or result the string `$ref:NAME` is the version bound earlier, and {\"$repeat\":[text,count],\"$suffix\":text} is a long string. A result string `$bind:NAME` binds a commit version (a canonical decimal u64 above zero) and `$bind:NAME>OTHER` also requires it to exceed OTHER. Versions are commit sequences and are never pinned as literals."
  ],
